# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What GitHub gets: exactly the tree the container image is built from, plus
# the files a repository needs to be publishable. Nothing else.
#
# WHITELIST, not blacklist -- `*` first, then re-include. The working tree is
# ~19 GB and grows a directory every few weeks; a blacklist has to be edited
# each time and its failure mode is silent, which is how 1.2 MB of build log,
# 119 files of packaged mirror, and 68 files hard-coding a home directory path
# reached a public repository in the first place.
#
# Git will not re-include a file whose PARENT DIRECTORY is still excluded, so
# each directory is re-included before its contents are filtered. Verify with
# `git ls-files` after any edit here: 27 files, and no tracked file quoting an
# absolute home-directory path.
#
# Everything excluded here still exists on disk. This file changes what is
# PUBLISHED, never what is kept.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

*

# ---- publication surface ----
!.gitignore
!.dockerignore
!Dockerfile
!LICENSE
!CITATION.cff
!.github/
!.github/README.md

# ---- the app ----
!.Rprofile
!app.R

# ---- the analysis engine: the 12 files app.R actually sources ----
# The other 23 files in R/ are CLI pipeline drivers that built the data. They
# are not in the app's source() closure, 10 of them hard-code an absolute home
# directory, and none of them can run without the >10 GB raw tree. Kept on
# disk, not published.
!R/
R/*
!R/about.R
!R/brand.R
!R/cptac.R
!R/data_access.R
!R/depmap.R
!R/guide.R
!R/plots.R
!R/registry.R
!R/rppa.R
!R/scan_lookup.R
!R/survival_engine.R
!R/tumor_normal.R

# ---- the cohort registry: the single source of truth for what exists ----
!config/
!config/*
# ...but not the pre-edit copy sitting beside it. It is a snapshot of the registry
# from before the colon panel was added; publishing it would put two registries in
# the tree with no statement of which one is current.
config/*.bak_*

# ---- branding assets the About page and the favicon render ----
!www/
!www/*

# ---- the one script the image runs ----
# scripts/ holds 72 files, 45 of which hard-code an absolute home directory.
# Only the build's self-check belongs in a published tree.
!scripts/
scripts/*
!scripts/docker_selfcheck.R
